# fixedbugs, defect 2555, lane b38-module, 2026-11-15.
#
# A fetched package's header embedding a file of the program's by a climb
# out of its root, `#embed "../../outside.bin"`. clang's `-M` writes the
# target whole, its climb kept, and the filesystem places it outside the
# root too, so C2 refuses it before anything compiles, the file named as
# clang wrote it: the repair that places a whole row by the filesystem lets
# no climb through. Needs clang 19 or later, which knows `#embed`.
use <pk>/pk

function main()
    print(pk.first())
